Done. Here's what I implemented:

SmartEditTool whitespace auto-fix — when edit_file fails because the old_text has the right content but wrong indentation, the tool now fixes it automatically instead of just hinting the AI to re-read the file.

**What changed in src/tool_wrappers.rs:**

1. `extract_matched_text()` — new helper that pulls exact lines from file content at a given 0-indexed line position for a given line count.

2. **`try_whitespace_autofix()** — new method on SmartEditTool` that:
   • Reads the file and runs `find_nearest_match`
   • If is_ws_only is false, returns None (not our problem)
   • Extracts the actual text from the file at the match position
   • Builds corrected params with the file's real whitespace
   • Retries the inner tool — on success, appends "⚡ Auto-fixed whitespace mismatch at line N"
   • On retry failure, returns None to fall through to the existing augmented error path

3. `execute()` — now calls try_whitespace_autofix() before `augment_not_found_error()`, so whitespace mismatches get fixed in one tool call instead of wasting a round-trip.

4. 7 new tests: 4 for `extract_matched_text` (basic, from-start, beyond-end, out-of-bounds) and 3 for auto-fix behavior (success, non-whitespace fallback, retry-failure fallback).
